      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\ud83d\udcdd ANNOTATION \u2014 open questions:\n\n\u2022 Should session-end be idempotent for the same commit SHA?\n  (currently it processes each SHA once and deletes)\n\n\u2022 How to handle transcript > LLM context window?\n  Current: truncate to most recent tokens\n\n\u2022 Should rocky explore auto-refresh after N days?\n\n\u2022 Should layer-1 dedup use cosine similarity instead of\n  prompt injection? (more reliable but needs embeddings)\n\n\u2022 Should there be a rocky session-end --dry-run mode?",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "twbozd1a",
      "originalText": "\ud83d\udcdd ANNOTATION \u2014 open questions:\n\n\u2022 Should session-end be idempotent for the same commit SHA?\n  (currently it processes each SHA once and deletes)\n\n\u2022 How to handle transcript > LLM context window?\n  Current: truncate to most recent tokens\n\n\u2022 Should rocky explore auto-refresh after N days?\n\n\u2022 Should layer-1 dedup use cosine similarity instead of\n  prompt injection? (more reliable but needs embeddings)\n\n\u2022 Should there be a rocky session-end --dry-run mode?",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    }
